  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEFRA_Biodiverse Landscape Fund_Cameroon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Plan is subbing to ZSL and will focus on two of the seven components, livelihoods and health; and will be implementing activities in Cameroon, Republic of Congo and Gabon. Our livelihoods component focuses on reducing the strains and stresses of the Western Congo Basin rainforest by providing alternative livelihood solutions that focus on non-forest timber products, including green microfinance, seed distribution, tree planting and also a more environmentally friendly cookstove distribution. Our health component focuses on SRHR and maternal and infant health. Training nurses on adolescent SRHR and maternal and infant feeding practices, as well as providing safe spaces for adolescents and lots of community engagement to combat harmful practices and cultural norms which contribute to high maternal and infant mortality rates (for example, a push to ensure women give birth in facilities, education on vector-borne diseases etc).</narrative>
  </description>
